---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About ExamHub.pk | Trusted Exam Preparation Platform"
  description="Learn about ExamHub.pk's mission to provide accessible, high-quality competitive exam preparation resources for Pakistani students."
>
  <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-900 via-slate-800 to-teal-950 text-white py-12">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">About ExamHub.pk</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-slate-300">
        Empowering Pakistani competitive exam candidates with syllabus-aligned learning tools.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 prose prose-lg prose-slate">
    <h2>Our Mission</h2>
    <p>
      ExamHub.pk was founded to democratize competitive exam preparation for candidates across all provinces of Pakistan. Whether aspiring for the Federal Civil Superior Services (CSS), Provincial Management Services (PMS), public service commissions (FPSC, PPSC, KPPSC, SPSC, BPSC), or university admissions via NTS, every student deserves access to accurate, well-explained study materials without restrictive paywalls.
    </p>

    <h2>What We Provide</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Curated Subject Collections:</strong> Over 70,000 multiple-choice questions categorized across 43 academic and professional subjects, each accompanied by step-by-step rationales.</li>
      <li><strong>Official Syllabus Alignment:</strong> Blueprint-based practice modules matching announced commission test patterns (e.g. FIA Assistant Director, FPSC Lecturers, Medical Officers, Civil Engineers).</li>
      <li><strong>Comprehensive Study Guides:</strong> Detailed analytical guides covering precis writing, current affairs, Islamic studies, and general science and ability.</li>
      <li><strong>Interactive Testing Engine:</strong> Real-time self-assessment mode featuring timed mock tests, instant feedback, question palette navigation, and bookmarking.</li>
      <li><strong>Continuous Content Quality Audits:</strong> Ongoing verification of answer keys against authoritative textbooks and official commission answer keys.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Our Editorial Board</h2>
    <p>
      ExamHub.pk's content is managed and reviewed by experienced educators, subject specialists, and former competitive exam qualifiers who understand the syllabus depth and pattern nuances required by Pakistani examination boards. We actively audit and refine question explanations to demystify distractor options and highlight underlying conceptual principles.
    </p>

    <h2>Why Candidates Trust ExamHub.pk</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Substantive Explanations:</strong> We believe answering an MCQ is only valuable when you understand <em>why</em> an answer is correct and why other choices are distractors.</li>
      <li><strong>Localized for Pakistan:</strong> Specialized focus on Pakistani constitution, history, administrative structures, regional geopolitics, and provincial curricula.</li>
      <li><strong>Accessible Learning:</strong> Openly accessible web and mobile resources designed to bridge the opportunity gap between urban academy centers and rural self-study candidates.</li>
      <li><strong>Distraction-Free Experience:</strong> Fast-loading, mobile-friendly interface designed with accessible typography and clean layouts so students can concentrate on study.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Covered Examination Bodies</h2>
    <p>
      Our practice modules and guides cover tests conducted by:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Federal Public Service Commission (FPSC) & CSS Competitive Examination</li>
      <li>Punjab Public Service Commission (PPSC) & PMS Punjab</li>
      <li>Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Public Service Commission (KPPSC)</li>
      <li>Sindh Public Service Commission (SPSC)</li>
      <li>Balochistan Public Service Commission (BPSC)</li>
      <li>National Testing Service (NTS), ETEA, and Higher Education Commission (HEC) tests</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact & Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      We welcome feedback, question suggestions, and corrections from students and educators alike. Please visit our <a href="/contact">Contact Page</a> or email our academic support team at <a href="mailto:support@examhub.pk">support@examhub.pk</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
